<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenian bank Hmezad 1996 net slumps.</title>
<headline>Slovenian bank Hmezad 1996 net slumps.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenian bank Hmezad Banka said on Friday 1996 net profit fell to 28.8 million tolars ($182,973) from 105.6 million in 1995 but expects the current year to swing back to around 100 million tolars.</p>
<p>Balance sheet assets rose to 10.1 billion tolars from 8.6 billion in the previous year.</p>
<p>Hmezad proposes paying a dividend, although the exact amount has yet to be determined. For 1995, Hmezad paid a 1,463 tolars dividend.</p>
<p>-- Novica Mihajlovic, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
<p>($=157 Slovenian Tolars)</p>
